For transmission minima (destructive interference in transmitted light):
2\mu t = (2n - 1)\frac{\lambda}{2}
Change in thickness between consecutive minima:
\Delta t = \frac{\lambda}{2\mu} = \frac{560 \times 10^{-9}}{2 \times 1.4} = 200 \times 10^{-9}\text{ m} = 2 \times 10^{-7}\text{ m}
This thickness decrease happens in \Delta \tau = 12\text{ s}.

Area of the film:
A = \pi r^2 = \pi (1.8 \times 10^{-2}\text{ m})^2 = 3.24\pi \times 10^{-4}\text{ m}^2
Rate of evaporation:
\text{Rate} = \frac{A \cdot \Delta t}{\Delta \tau} = \frac{3.24\pi \times 10^{-4} \times 2 \times 10^{-7}}{12} = \frac{6.48\pi \times 10^{-11}}{12} = 54\pi \times 10^{-13}\text{m}^3\text{ s}^{-1}

