Which of the following is/are not correct with respect to energy of atomic orbitals of hydrogen atom ?
(A) 1\text{s} < 2\text{p} < 3\text{d} < 4\text{s}
(B) 1\text{s} < 2\text{s} = 2\text{p} < 3\text{s} = 3\text{p}
(C) 1\text{s} < 2\text{s} < 2\text{p} < 3\text{s} < 3\text{p}
(D) 1\text{s} < 2\text{s} < 4\text{s} < 3\text{d}
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :

questions.solution:
For hydrogen atom (single electron species), energy depends ONLY on principal quantum number n:
1\text{s} < 2\text{s} = 2\text{p} < 3\text{s} = 3\text{p} = 3\text{d} < 4\text{s} = 4\text{p} = 4\text{d} = 4\text{f}
Therefore, statements (C) and (D) are not correct.

